Selected Idea
-------------

How to choose the right way to install gh on Linux: official packages, community builds, and one strongly discouraged path
The source cleanly divides installation methods into three classes-Recommended (official Debian/RPM/Homebrew/precompiled), Community (distribution-maintained or third-party packages), and Discouraged (Snap). A practical explainer can help readers decide which class to use based on support expectations and platform availability, using only the facts and warnings given in the document.

